# ============================================================
#  Minor chains: short cause-and-effect stories.
#    forbidden  — the Restricted Section key (from umbral_forbidden_notes)
#    curse      — curing the Umbral Curse
#    debt       — Grisk the moneylender (see state in_debt)
#    familiar   — Ember the fox-spirit
#    ghost      — the haunted dormitory
# ============================================================

# ---------------- The Restricted Section ----------------
# Feedback 2026-10-16: the key (umbral_forbidden_notes) is a lead, and the chain is played by going there: each step is
# a card at the Restricted Section after hours (evening or midnight), waiting on the key and the step before.

@thread forbidden
from: story
with: begun=flag(forbidden_key)
clues: lead_codex_open lead_restricted_shelves lead_silver_key
members:
  start umbral_forbidden_notes

@event forbidden_annotations
title: Three Colours of Ink
place: library
class: story
tone: eerie
when: seen(forbidden_section_1) == 0 and not flag(forbidden_abandoned)
weight: 14
art: book
tags: mystery study
thread: forbidden
scene: A battered notebook open on a library desk, its margins crowded with notes in red, green and black ink, a silver key lying across the page.
text: You read Odile's notebook properly at last, at a desk within sight of the locked door. Black ink for the shelves, green for the prefects' rounds, red for warnings. Half the red is underlined twice.
> left: Learn the prefects' rounds
  hint: Easier to slip in unseen.
  guile +small
  flag forbidden_rounds
  say: Green ink: the prefect on library duty walks the east stacks at nine and the west at ten, and stops for tea in between. You learn it like a timetable.
> right: Learn the shelf marks
  hint: Know what not to touch.
  lore +small
  flag forbidden_shelfmarks
  say: Black ink and red: which shelves are safe, which books are bound in something that isn't leather, and, underlined twice, "never with bare hands".

@event forbidden_section_1
title: The Silver Key
class: story
tone: eerie
place: restricted_section
time: evening midnight
when: not flag(forbidden_inside) and not flag(forbidden_abandoned)
repeat: 3
weight: 16
art: key
tags: mystery
thread: forbidden
scene: A heavy iron door at the end of a library aisle, a silver key turning in its lock, a candle held low.
text: After hours. The silver key fits the Restricted Section door perfectly. Beyond it, shelves of black-bound books breathe softly in the dark. Somewhere, a prefect's footsteps.
> left: Turn back
  mood -tiny
  flag forbidden_abandoned
  say: You lock the door again and hang the key on a nail in your wardrobe. Some nights you hear it rattling.
> right: Slip inside
  challenge deceive apprentice+ +1 if flag(forbidden_rounds):
    win:
      lore +medium
      flag forbidden_inside
      find lead_restricted_shelves
      say: You spend two hours reading by candle-stub. You leave with a head full of things no student should know, and the certainty that you'll come back.
    lose:
      gain detention
      gain watched
      rel bram -medium
      say: Bram Hollis is waiting by the door when you come out. He is smiling. It's the worst smile you've ever seen.

@event forbidden_bram_watch
title: The Prefect at the Door
class: story
tone: tense
place: restricted_section
time: evening midnight
when: seen(forbidden_section_1) > 0 and not flag(forbidden_read) and not flag(forbidden_abandoned)
repeat: 4
weight: 12
actor: bram
art: lock
tags: mystery danger
thread: forbidden
scene: A broad prefect leaning against an iron library door with folded arms, a lantern at his feet, a student watching from behind a bookcase.
text: {Bram Hollis is leaning on the Restricted Section door, lantern at his feet, as if he has all night. Somebody has told him about the key, or he has guessed.|Bram is at the door again. He has brought a sandwich this time.|Bram's watch on the door has become a habit. He hums while he waits, badly.}
> left: Wait him out in the stacks
  hint: Cold and cramped, but unseen.
  health -tiny
  lore +small
  say: {You crouch behind the history shelves for an hour, reading by the light of his lantern, until he gives up and goes to bed.|You wait him out, and he eats the whole sandwich first. Your knees will never forgive you.|You know his humming now. When it stops, he's asleep on his feet, and you slip past.}
> right: Bluff your way past
  hint: Guile against a prefect who wants to catch you.
  challenge deceive vs bram.guile:
    win:
      guile +small
      say: {You tell him a professor is looking for him in the east tower. He goes. You are inside before his lantern reaches the stair.|"Thorne wants you," you say, and Bram's face goes pale. Nobody checks whether Thorne wants them.|You tell him there's a fight in the courtyard. There isn't. He's gone before you finish the sentence.}
    lose:
      gain watched
      rel bram -small
      say: {"Nice try," says Bram, and writes your name in his little book with great pleasure.|He laughs, actually laughs, and walks you back to your dormitory by the ear.|Bram has heard that one before, from you. He takes your name, and his time over it.}

@event forbidden_section_2
title: The Codex of Hollow Names
class: story
tone: eerie
place: restricted_section
time: evening midnight
when: flag(forbidden_inside) and not flag(forbidden_read) and since(forbidden_section_1) >= 1
repeat: 2
weight: 16
art: book
tags: mystery hollowstar
thread: forbidden
scene: A book bound in something that is not leather, open on a reading stand, its letters slowly rearranging themselves.
text: You keep going back. One night, a book finds you. It falls from a high shelf and lands open at your feet: the Codex of Hollow Names. The first page is a list of names. The last one is still being written. It's yours.{flag(forbidden_warned):  Odile's warning comes back to you: don't let a book choose you.|}
> left: Put it back
  mood -tiny
  say: You shelve it. When you look back, it has fallen again, open at the same page.
> right: Read it
  lore +medium
  arcana +medium
  alignment -tiny
  find codex_names
  flag forbidden_read
  find lead_codex_open
  chance even -1 if flag(forbidden_shelfmarks):
    gain umbral_curse
    say: You read until dawn. You learn about the thing under the lake. When you finally close the book, your fingertips are grey.
  else:
    say: You read until dawn and close the book with shaking hands. Some things you can't unread.

@event forbidden_fourth_year
title: Odile's Last Week
place: library
class: story
tone: warm
when: seen(forbidden_section_1) > 0 and seen(forbidden_section_3) == 0
weight: 14
art: book
tags: mystery social
thread: forbidden
scene: A fourth-year with a packed satchel leaning on a library shelf, talking quietly to a younger student between the stacks.
text: Odile Varn finds you between the stacks with her satchel already packed. She leaves at the end of term. "You used the key," she says. It isn't a question. "I won't ask what you found. Unless you want to tell me."
> left: Tell her what you've seen
  hint: She has a warning for you.
  mood +small
  flag forbidden_warned
  say: She listens to all of it, then puts a hand on your notebook. "Some books want readers," she says. "If one falls open at your feet, don't let it choose you." Then she hugs you, briefly, and is gone.
> right: Keep it to yourself
  hint: Your secret stays yours.
  guile +small
  say: She smiles, as if that were the right answer. "Good," she says. "That's how I kept it too." She leaves you her spare candle-stubs and a list of the quietest desks.

@event forbidden_section_3
title: Caught
class: story
tone: eerie
place: restricted_section
time: evening midnight
when: flag(forbidden_read) and since(forbidden_section_2) >= 1
weight: 16
actor: isolde
art: lock
tags: mystery
thread: forbidden
scene: A tall silhouette in the doorway of the Restricted Section, holding a lantern that casts long shadows over a startled student.
text: A lantern blazes in the doorway. Not a prefect this time: the headmistress herself. She looks at the book in your hands, then at you, for a very long time. "Most students who find that book," she says, "don't put it down."
> left: Apologise and accept punishment
  alignment +small
  meet isolde
  study -medium
  gain detention
  rel isolde +small
  unflag forbidden_key
  say: She takes the key. "Detention, every evening this month; your coursework can wait. And come to my tower on Thursdays. If you're going to learn dangerous things, you'll learn them properly."
> right: Ask her what it means
  meet isolde
  rel isolde +medium
  lore +medium
  find codex_names
  unflag forbidden_key
  say: A long pause. "It means something is waking, and it is looking for help. Make sure it doesn't find yours." She takes the key, leaves you the candle, and forgets, or chooses to forget, the detention.

# ---------------- The Umbral Curse ----------------

@thread curse
from: story
with: begun=flag(moonpetal_sought)
when: has(umbral_curse)
clues: lead_moonpetal
members:
  start curse_cure_1

@event curse_cure_1
title: A Cold That Won't Leave
class: story
tone: grim
when: not flag(moonpetal_sought)
repeat: 6
weight: 30
art: skull
tags: crisis mystery
thread: curse
scene: A student wrapped in three blankets beside a roaring fire, breath still fogging the air, fingertips grey.
text: {&The cold under your skin is getting worse.|The cold is back, worse than before.} Sister Amaranth's tonics do nothing. She looks troubled. "This isn't an illness. It's a hunger." She lowers her voice. "Old Maud might know something. Don't tell anyone I said so."
> left: Endure it
  mood -tiny
  arcana +tiny
  say: You pile on blankets and keep going. The cold whispers sometimes. You pretend not to hear. Maud, you suppose, will still be there if it gets worse.
> right: Go to Old Maud
  meet maud
  rel maud +small
  flag moonpetal_sought
  find lead_moonpetal
  say: Maud takes one look at your fingertips and puts the kettle on. "Moonpetal," she says. "Grows in the Whisperwood. Only blooms after dark. You'll fetch it yourself — the cure has to come from the cursed."

@event curse_cure_2
title: Moonpetal
class: story
tone: tense
place: whisperwood
slot: evening
repeat: 6
weight: 60
art: flower
tags: nature danger
thread: curse
scene: A dark forest at nightfall, a single silver flower glowing in a clearing, eyes watching from between the trees.
text: The Whisperwood after dark. Things move between the trees. In a clearing, a single silver flower is opening, and between you and it stands a stag made of shadow.
> left: Sneak around it
  challenge deceive journeyman:
    win:
      lose umbral_curse
      rel maud +medium
      say: You creep through the bracken and pluck the moonpetal. Maud's brew tastes like moonlight and burnt sugar. The cold is gone.
    lose:
      health -large
      say: The stag sees you. You run. No moonpetal tonight; you'll have to come back.
> right: Face the stag
  challenge combat adept-:
    win:
      lose umbral_curse
      vigor +small
      rel maud +medium
      say: You stand your ground. The stag lowers its head — and steps aside. Maud's brew drives the cold out of your bones.
    lose:
      health -large
      say: The stag charges. You wake up in the bracken at dawn. Maud bandages you. "Another night," she says.

# ---------------- Grisk the Moneylender ----------------

@thread debt

@event grisk_offer
title: A Helpful Goblin
class: story
tone: tense
when: gold < 15 and turn >= 3 and not has(in_debt) and not flag(grisk_done)
weight: 30
art: pouch
tags: money danger
thread: debt
scene: A small goblin in a velvet waistcoat and pince-nez, sitting on a crate in an alley, a ledger in one hand and a quill behind his ear.
text: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat falls into step beside you. "Grisk," he says, "friend to the temporarily embarrassed. Sixty crowns, today. Twelve a month for six months. Very reasonable."
> left: No thank you
  meet grisk
  mood -tiny
  say: "My door is always open," Grisk says. You suspect it is actually always locked.
> right: Take the loan
  meet grisk
  gold +huge
  gain in_debt
  debt_paid = 0
  debt_missed = 0
  flag grisk_done
  say: He counts out sixty crowns, writes your name in the ledger and smiles with a great many teeth.

@event grisk_board_debt
title: Settled, With Interest
class: incident
tone: tense
trigger: queued
priority: 70
art: pouch
tags: money danger
thread: debt
scene: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat waiting outside the bursar's office, waving a receipt like a small flag.
text: The bursar's office has stopped sending reminders. Instead, Grisk is waiting outside it with a receipt. "Two months' board, paid in full," he beams. "By me. A loan, naturally, with a little extra for your pocket. Twelve a month for six months. You can sign here."
> left: Sign his ledger
  meet grisk
  gold +large
  gold +medium
  gain in_debt
  debt_paid = 0
  debt_missed = 0
  flag grisk_done
  say: You sign. He has already paid the board out of it; he counts the rest into your palm and writes your name in the ledger with a flourish that has teeth in it.
> right: Beg the bursar for time
  meet grisk
  flag grisk_done
  mood -small
  renown -tiny
  say: You spend an afternoon on a hard bench outside the bursar's office and leave with a month's grace and the feeling of having been looked at over spectacles for a very long time.

@event grisk_favour
title: Grisk's Proposition
class: story
tone: eerie
when: has(in_debt)
weight: 14
art: chain
tags: money mystery
thread: debt
scene: The goblin moneylender leaning close in a library alcove, pushing a slip of paper across a table.
text: Grisk finds you in the library. "I could cancel your debt," he murmurs. "A small favour. There's a book in the archive — the Founders' Ledger. A client wants a page. Just one page."
> left: Refuse
  alignment +tiny
  say: "Pity." He makes a note in his ledger. It looks expensive.
> right: Do the favour
  alignment -small
  challenge deceive apprentice+:
    win:
      lose in_debt
      flag grisk_favour
      say: You razor a page from the oldest ledger in the archive. Grisk tears up your debt. You notice the page had a black star on it.
    lose:
      gain detention
      study -medium
      say: The archivist catches you with a razor in your hand. Detention. Grisk is nowhere to be found, and the debt stands.

@event grisk_smuggling
time: afternoon evening
title: One More Job
class: story
tone: tense
when: flag(grisk_favour) and not has(in_debt)
weight: 10
art: pouch
tags: money danger
thread: debt
scene: A crate of clinking bottles hidden under a tarp on a dark boathouse dock, a small goblin silhouetted against the lake.
text: Grisk again. "You were so good last time. I have parcels that need carrying: collected at the boathouse at midnight, delivered to the village by day. Thirty crowns a parcel. Steady work, for steady hands."
> left: You're done with him
  unflag grisk_favour
  flag grisk_gone
  mood +small
  say: "Everyone's done with me eventually," Grisk says, without rancour. You never see him again.
> right: Hear him out
  flag grisk_contact
  find lead_grisk_jetty
  alignment -tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: He explains the arrangement: the jetty, midnight, oilcloth, a cobbler's back door. "Any month you like," he says. "I'm very flexible." You walk away with the arrangement in your head, and it won't leave.

# ---------------- Ember the Fox-Spirit ----------------

@thread familiar

@event fox_injured
title: Smoke in the Woods
class: story
tone: light
when: turn >= 4 and not flag(fox_met)
weight: 6 + flag(familiar_affinity) * 14
art: fox
tags: nature
thread: familiar
scene: A small red fox lying in the snow at the forest edge, its tail smouldering like a dying campfire, one paw caught in a rusted snare.
text: At the edge of the forest, a thin plume of smoke. A small fox is caught in a rusted snare, its tail smouldering like an ember. It snarls at you, then whimpers.
> left: Leave it — it's wild
  mood -tiny
  say: You walk away. That night you dream of smoke.
> right: Free it and bandage the paw
  flag fox_met
  health -tiny
  alignment +tiny
  queue fox_returns in 2
  say: It bites you, of course. But it lets you wrap the paw. Then it limps into the trees, glancing back once with eyes like embers.

@event fox_returns
title: A Visitor at the Window
class: story
tone: light
trigger: queued
art: fox
tags: nature
thread: familiar
scene: A fox with a softly glowing tail sitting on a stone windowsill at dawn, a ruby glinting at its feet.
text: Two months later, a fox with a glowing tail is sitting on your windowsill. Its paw has healed. At its feet: a small, dusty ruby.
> left: Shoo it away
  gold +medium
  say: It leaves the ruby and vanishes. You sell the ruby. Somehow you feel you've failed a test.
> right: Open the window
  gold +medium
  mood +small
  queue fox_bond in 1
  say: It hops in, inspects your room thoroughly and falls asleep on your pillow. Your pillow is now slightly scorched. You don't mind.

@event fox_bond
title: Ember
class: story
tone: light
trigger: queued
art: fox
tags: nature magic
thread: familiar
scene: A student and a small fire-tailed fox nose to nose, a soft golden light connecting them.
text: The fox has decided. {term: It follows you to class|It follows you through the half-empty corridors}, sleeps on your feet and growls at Bram. Students aren't allowed unregistered familiars. Registering one costs fifteen crowns.
> left: Hide her
  challenge deceive apprentice:
    win:
      gain familiar_fox
      say: You name her Ember. Nobody notices a fox that doesn't want to be noticed.
    lose:
      gain familiar_fox
      gold -medium
      say: A professor spots her at once. You pay what you can of the fee — and Ember is yours, officially.
> right: Register her properly
  gold -medium
  gain familiar_fox
  rel isolde +tiny
  say: The registrar stamps a form. "Name?" "Ember," you say. The fox looks smug.

@event fox_helps
title: Ember Finds Something
class: story
tone: light
when: has(familiar_fox)
weight: 10
repeat: 8
art: fox
tags: nature
thread: familiar
scene: A fox nosing through dry leaves under a hedge and emerging with a purse in its jaws.
text: {~Ember drags you, by the sleeve, through three corridors and a hedge. She's found something. She's very proud of it.|Ember sits on your book until you look at her. She has found something, and she has buried it, and now she wants you to dig.|Ember comes back from the lake with her tail steaming and something in her jaws. She drops it at your feet like a gift.}
> left: Let her keep it
  mood +small
  say: {~It's a sock. Ember is thrilled. You are thrilled for her.|It's a glove that smells of the stables. Ember sleeps on it for a week.|It's a pine cone, slightly charred. She guards it from Bram personally.}
> right: See what it is
  chance even:
    gold +medium
    say: A lost purse. You return it to its owner, who insists you keep the reward.
  else:
    lore +small
    say: A lost page from a professor's lecture notes. Enlightening.

# ---------------- The Haunted Dormitory ----------------

@thread ghost

@event ghost_socks
time: morning
title: Rearranged Socks
class: story
tone: eerie
when: turn >= 3 and not flag(ghost_met)
weight: 8
art: ghost
tags: mystery
thread: ghost
scene: A dormitory drawer open in candlelight, socks arranged in a careful spiral, a faint shimmer in the air above them.
text: Every morning, your socks have been rearranged. By colour. Then alphabetically by colour. Last night they spelled out "HELP".
> left: Ignore it
  gain haunted
  say: You buy new socks. The next morning they're arranged by mood.
> right: Stay up and watch
  flag ghost_met
  gain haunted
  queue ghost_reveal now
  say: At three in the morning, the drawer slides open by itself.

@event ghost_reveal
title: Prudence
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: queued
art: ghost
tags: mystery
thread: ghost
scene: A translucent girl in old-fashioned school robes, hovering by a window, holding a faded letter.
text: A girl in old-fashioned robes, translucent and very polite. "Prudence Ashworth, class of 1793. Terribly sorry about the socks. I never finished my letter. Could you deliver it? The village. The bakery. Please."
> left: Exorcise her
  lose haunted
  alignment -tiny
  arcana +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: You speak the banishing rite. She fades with a small, hurt look. Your socks stay put after that. You feel a bit rotten.
> right: Promise to deliver it
  queue ghost_letter in 1
  say: She claps her translucent hands. "Oh, thank you! It's only taken two hundred years."

@event ghost_letter
title: A Letter Two Hundred Years Late
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: queued
art: letter
tags: mystery social
scene: A cosy village bakery, an old baker reading a yellowed letter with tears on her cheeks, a ghostly figure smiling in the doorway.
text: The bakery has been in the same family for two hundred years. The old baker reads Prudence's letter at the counter. "My great-great-great-grandmother waited for this," she says. "She never stopped."
> left: Stay and listen to the story
  lose haunted
  mood +large
  lore +small
  say: Prudence was in love with the baker's daughter. When you return, the ghost is waiting, glowing like a sunrise. Then she's gone, at peace.
> right: Leave quietly
  lose haunted
  mood +medium
  renown +small
  say: The baker presses a free loaf into your hands. That night, your socks are arranged into a heart. Then never again.
